aphically first root, or use the set of roots. The spec states\n56\t   which IK and IL goldens move. The AMIE run-of-record outcomes must not\n57\t   change: neither staffing run joins through a subtype. That is a test.\n58\t2. **IL4-Q2, the binding.** Choices: add `export_sha256` within\n59\t   `gnd-mined-run/1` as a required field (every retained `reported.json` is\n60\t   re-derived and IL6's shipped `staffing/learners/*/reported.json` and its\n61\t   walk goldens move), or bump to `/2` and keep a `/1` reader. The ruled\n62\t   re-derivation is mechanical: the digest is already recorded in each run's\n63\t   `outcome.json`. No learner run.\n64\t3. **IL1-Q1.** The IK5 goldens that move are listed, with each refusal it\n65\t   adds. An infix comparison on a variable of the wrong type becomes\n66\t   `type-confused-join`.\n67\t4. **IL2-Q3.** An off-threshold constant becomes a named refusal from the ASP\n68\t   reader. ILASP's retained run is unchanged: its refusal,\n69\t   `empty-antecedent`, comes first.\n70\t5. **IL6-Q2.** `tools/ilp_comparison.py` exits non-zero and names the rule.\n71\t   This needs a test with a planted unmappable rule.\n72\t6. **The comparison stays true.** After Part A, `tools/ilp_comparison.py`\n73\t   still reproduces `comparison.json` and the walk page still passes 12\n74\t   blocks, or the spec names every row or digest that moves, and why.\n75\t\n76\tGate: IL6's gate files plus the new tests; T9 (both wheel origins) once,\n77\tbecause shipped files may move under IL4-Q2.\n78\t\n79\t## Part B: plan repairs (proposed wording)\n80\t\n81\tThe plan file is `notes/ilp-learners-plan.md`. Each repair is a wording change\n82\tthat records what happened. None changes an approved criterion's intent.\n83\t\n84\t| Row | Where | Now | Proposed |\n85\t|---|---|---|---|\n86\t| IL3-Q4 | §1, line 43 | \"Boolean rule sets (integer-programming or certifiable rule-set learners)\" | \"Boolean rule sets (a sequential-covering learner, RIPPER, IL3-D1 (a); integer-programming and certifiable learners were not integrated)\" |\n87\t| IL4-Q5 | §4 IL6, line 104 | the walk \"runs the IK6 refunds example through\" every adapter | labelled adapters on the refunds example; `amie` on the committed staffing fixture, which has the relations a miner needs |\n88\t| IL4-Q5 | §4 IL4, line 358 | \"the miner's positive-example count\" | \"the miner's support, its count of distinct head pairs\" (AMIE prints no positive examples; IL4-F4) |\n89\t| IL2-Q4 | §0 IL-R9 | \"the learner's own timeout below the wall clock\" | add: \"where the learner has one; ILASP 4.4.1 and the agent CLIs have none, so `learner-timeout` is unreachable there and the wall clock is the bound\" |\n90\t| IL1-Q7 | §9 IL1 row, line 660 | \"goldens unchanged except listed C2 cases\" | \"goldens unchanged except the C2 cases and the IK5 goldens named by the owner-recorded amendments\" |\n91\t| IL6 refuted premise 2 | §5, line 583 | \"the two pin sites\" | \"the pin sites: gnd-export, gnd-model-evolve, and gnd-solve's Station 6 (IL6 review R3)\" |\n92\t| Plan status line | line 3 | \"Draft; awaiting owner approval\" | approved as recorded in `001-plan-gate.md` (approval was recorded there, not in the plan) |\n93\t\n94\t## Part D: the close review\n95\t\n96\tThe four-reviewer bar (plan §8). Run through the maintained panel, which\n97\tneeds the parent credentials; the launcher is\n98\t`uv run python tools/run_gnd_review_panel.py`. The input is the close bundle:\n99\tthe plan with its repairs, records `002` to `008`, the close record draft, and\n100\tthe milestone diff `07f4d45^..HEAD`. The stop rule in\n101\t`process-phase/references/review-convergence.md` bounds the number of rounds.\n102\t\n103\t## Order\n104\t\n105\tA (spec, then STOP for the owner gate, implement, review, record) → B → C →\n106\tD → E. B and C can be written while A is in review. They are recorded only\n107\tonce A's record exists, because A changes some rows' dispositions."}
