L2-D14 (a) rulings from the review, spec §14.\n86\t\n87\t**The headline.** In invocation 1, a real ILASP 4.4.1 learned this from GND's\n88\trefunds export in 123.7 s:\n89\t\n90\t```\n91\twrong :- gt_t_amount(V1,500).\n92\t```\n93\t\n94\tGND refused it: `refused:empty-antecedent`, exit 3. The rule names only the\n95\tcomparison, so there is no antecedent atom for a guarded constraint. Its\n96\tmeaning is right: clingo, evaluating it independently over the task, covers\n97\tharbor, market, airport and station, the four weeks Popper's IL1 rule\n98\tcovers. This is IL2-F7, a property of the rendering, and the owner ruled it\n99\ta recorded result rather than a defect to amend.\n100\t\n101\t## What shipped\n102\t\n103\t- **`gnd.export.ilp_asp`** (new, export lane):\n104\t  - `render` writes `ilasp/task.las`. The background is the comparison\n105\t    definitions only: per integer type, `dom_t` rules over the predicates,\n106\t    `thr_t` facts from IL1's threshold selection, and `gt_t`/`lt_t` rules.\n107\t    Then the `#constant`s, `#modeh(wrong)`, one `#modeb` per predicate\n108\t    (without the example argument) and per comparison, `#maxv(4)`, and one\n109\t    `#pos`/`#neg` context per labelled example, ids `e<i>`.\n110\t  - It refuses as `unrepresentable`: a string with a control character\n111\t    other than a newline, and (IL2-D14) an integer outside clingo's 32-bit\n112\t    range.\n113\t  - `extract_hypothesis` takes every non-blank line after ILASP's last\n114\t    `%%` line (IL2-F5, then IL2-F8).\n115\t  - `parse_hypothesis` is a closed, capped reader to `gnd-ilp-clauses/1`:\n116\t    11 named refusals, `unparsable` with line and column for everything\n117\t    else (including what clingo reads differently, IL2-F9, and bare\n118\t    symbolic constants, IL2-D13), and `wrong :- body.` threaded to\n119\t    `wrong(X) :- body'`.\n120\t- **The registry entry `ilasp`** (`method: ilp-ilasp`, run-record learner\n121\t  `ilasp`, adapter version 1, `boolean_strings` false). Check 9 now refuses a\n122\t  quoted `\"true\"`/`\"false\"` on a boolean role for this entry only (IL2-D13).\n123\t- **IL2-D8 in `ilp_popper`:** threshold names the renderer never writes\n124\t  (leading zeros, `m0`, `m` with a leading zero) are `unparsable`.\n125\t- **Shared homes in `gnd.export.ilp`** (step 5): `observed_integers`,\n126\t  `COMPARISON_NAME`, `refusal_name`.\n127\t- **Surfaces:** both CLI `choices` tuples and both schema `target` enums add\n128\t  `ilasp` within `/1`; `docs/reference/ilp-bridge.md` gains the ILASP\n129\t  section; `tools/gnd_layers.json` assigns the module.\n130\t- **The evidence script** `evidence/IL2/run_ilasp.py`: ILASP under\n131\t  `run_bounded_process` (600 s wall clock, 10 s grace, output caps), clingo\n132\t  as the independent coverage evaluator, fixed import arguments, path\n133\t  sanitization, and `--complete-retained` for IL2-F6.\n134\t\n135\t**Goldens that moved:** 9 RF1 CLI goldens (the export and import help and\n136\texit files, and the two `target` actions of `cli/tree.json`, patched in\n137\tplace, IL2-F3). Every IK5, IK6 and IL1 golden and every Popper rendering is\n138\tbyte-identical. The approved corpus answer for `k4-symbolic` changed by the\n139\tIL2-D13 ruling; the case keeps its prior answer.\n140\t\n141\t## Gate output (verbatim)\n142\t\n143\tFrom `evidence/IL2/final-gate.txt`, at `3f34325` (the scratch path replaced\n144\tby `<scratch>`):\n145\t\n146\t```\n147\t$ uv run pytest -q -p no:randomly $(cat .gnd-planning/milestones/ilp-learners/evidence/IL2/gate-files.txt)\n148\t766 passed, 20 deselected in 47.77s\n149\texit 0\n150\t$ GND_IL2_CLINGO_PYTHON=<scratch>/il1-live/venv/bin/python uv run pytest -q -p no:randomly -m live tests/test_ilp_asp.py\n151\t1 passed, 89 deselected in 0.53s\n152\texit 0\n153\t$ uv run ruff check src/gnd/export tests/test_ilp_asp.py tests/test_ilp_learners.py .gnd-planning/milestones/ilp-learners/evidence/IL2/run_ilasp.py\n154\tAll checks passed!\n155\texit 0\n156\t```\n157\t\n158\tEvery regression test for a review fix was observed red against `bf15642`\n159\t(18 failed, 13 passed), and the IL2-D13/D14 tests against `58704ed`'s code\n160\t(7 failed, 1 passed), before their fixes.\n161\t\n162\t## The run of record\n163\t\n164\t| Invocation | Termination | Import | What it settled |\n165\t|---|---|---|---|\n166\t| 1, **the run of record** | `completed` (123.7 s by ILASP's own timing; the process record was lost, IL2-F6) | `refused:empty-antecedent` | ILASP accepts the rendering; it prefers the lone comparison, which GND's fragment refuses (IL2-F7) |\n167\t\n168\tT9 replays it from its committed bytes in the default gate: E, the\n169\textraction, the import's exit and its refusal line. The null process record\n170\tis accepted only for invocation 1 and only with the IL2-F6 note.\n171\t\n172\t**The spec's three live-run questions** (§6):\n173\t1. **Does ILASP accept the rendering?** Yes.\n174\t2. **Does the hypothesis parse and import?** It parses; the checker refuses\n175\t   it as `empty-antecedent`.\n176\t3. **Does clingo's coverage agree with GND's?** GND computed none, because\n177\t   the clause was refused before support. clingo's covered set equals GND's\n178\t   for Popper's equivalent rule.\n179\t\n180\t## Criteria\n181\t\n182\t| Criterion | Result |\n183\t|---|---|\n184\t| IL2-C1 ASP golden | holds: T1 (refunds and the IK5 X1 model, `PYTHONHASHSEED` 0 and 1, byte-identical), T1b (background is comparisons only, contexts without the example argument, `#modeb` arity = arity − 1, thresholds = IL1's selection) |\n185\t| IL2-C2 reader | holds: T3 (the fixture hypothesis to its clause JSON), T4 (one case per refusal name, 11), T4b (`not` and aggregates reach the checker's names), T5 (one case per constants row), T6 and the R cases (totality and caps), T12 (both doc tables pinned to the reader) |\n186\t| IL2-C3 shared binding | holds: T3 admits through the shared checker with `method: ilp-ilasp`; T7 (`learner-mismatch`, `coverage-mismatch`); T8 (`type-confused-join`) |\n187\t| IL2-C4 live run | holds: the licence was recorded (spec §12) and ruled (IL2-D1) before the download; invocation 1 has one termination and one import value; T9 replays it |\n188\t\n189\t**Plan §9's IL2 row** (\"ASP golden; per-construct refusals; replayed live\n190\trecord\", affecting \"new adapter tests; RF1 CLI goldens; schema enums\"): T1,\n191\tT4 and T9 respectively; the RF1 goldens moved as listed; T2 pins the enums.\n192\t\n193\t## Review\n194\t\n195\tOne local reviewer agent read `git diff 65fd6df bf15642`\n196\t([review note](notes/phase-IL2-agent-review.md)). It found 1 blocking, 6\n197\thardening and 4 completeness findings, all reproduced. The blocker\n198\t(IL2-F8: the extractor dropped learned constraints, and the clingo\n199\tcross-check saw the same truncated text) and 8 others were fixed with\n200\tregressions; findings 2 and 6's export half became IL2-D13 and IL2-D14 and\n201\twere implemented as ruled. Finding 5's off-threshold constant is a boundary\n202\trow.\n203\t\n204\t## Refactoring review\n205\t\n206\t**Executed** (spec §14, \"Step 5\"), behavior-preserving, behind the gate above:\n207\t1. **`observed_integers`:** the per-type integer collection was written out\n208\t   in both `ilp_popper._threshold_rows` and `ilp_asp._domains`.\n209\t2. **`COMPARISON_NAME`:** the comparison-name regex was written out in both\n210\t   readers.\n211\t3. **`refusal_name`:** learner-agnostic, so it moved out of the ILASP adapter.\n212\t\n213\t**Not refactored, argued:** IL1's `evidence/IL1/run_popper.py` keeps its own\n214\tcopy of the refusal parse; it is retained evidence cited by digest in the\n215\tIL1 record.\n216\t\n217\t**Carried from IL1:** IL1-Q2's two halves were re-targeted by IL2-D7:\n218\tnon-exporting entries to IL5, `contract` variation to IL4. IL2's entry\n219\texports and uses `labelled-clauses`, so neither became real here.\n220\t\n221\t## Boundary — what this phase does NOT establish\n222\t\n223\t- **One reviewer is one reviewer.**\n224\t  - The adversarial review was one local agent over `git diff 65fd6df bf15642`.\n225\t  - It did not run ILASP or the full suite.\n226\t  - The fixes, the IL2-D13/D14 code and the step 5 refactors carry no review\n227\t    opinion.\n228\t- **No admitted ILASP rule.** The one run produced a rule GND refuses.\n229\t  IL2 shows the bridge carries ILASP's output to a named verdict, not that\n230\t  ILASP's rules are admitted on this data.\n231\t- **Reproducibility is not measured.** Invocation 1 is a single run.\n232\t- **The process record of invocation 1 was lost** (IL2-F6). `completed` rests\n233\t  on the retained output: ILASP's closing `%% Total` block, 123.7 s below\n234\t  the 600 s wall clock, and output far below the caps. The exit status was\n235\t  not observed.\n236\t- **No learner timeout.** ILASP 4.4.1 has no timeout option, so\n237\t  `learner-timeout` is unreachable; the wall clock is the only limit (IL2-D3\n238\t  (a)).\n239\t- **An off-threshold comparison constant** (`gt_t_amount(V,501)` when 501 is\n240\t  not a rendered threshold) has no ASP meaning, and the reader cannot see the\n241\t  export to refuse it. Only a run record whose coverage comes from an\n242\t  independent evaluator, as `run_ilasp.py`'s does, refuses it\n243\t  (`coverage-mismatch`).\n244\t- **ILASP's other settings are not covered.** Only the spec §6 settings ran:\n245\t  no `-nc`, no noise, no other `--version`.\n246\t- **The ILASP binary runs on a scratch, non-framework CPython 3.10** through a\n247\t  framework-path shim (IL2-D12 (a)). Nothing about Homebrew's build is\n248\t  established.\n249\t- **Licences.** ILASP is used for non-commercial research by the owner's\n250\t  ruling (IL2-D1); nothing is distributed or committed from it.\n251\t- **Spec §6 listed 8 moved goldens; 9 moved** (IL2-F3).\n252\t- **The broad historical lane did not run** (`slow_cadence`).\n253\t\n254\t## Open questions\n255\t\n256\t| ID | Question | Origin | Target |\n257\t|---|---|---|---|\n258\t| IL2-Q1 | The Popper reader reads a bare `true` as the string `\"true\"`, while the Popper renderer writes a boolean bare | spec §7, ruled to carry | ilp-learners close |\n259\t| IL2-Q2 | Should the ILASP bias require each comparison variable to occur in a predicate atom (amendment IL2-A1, adapter 2, a second run)? | IL2-F7; the owner ruled invocation 1 as is | IL6 or a later evaluation phase |\n260\t| IL2-Q3 | Should the import hand the export's thresholds to the ASP reader, so an off-threshold constant is refused without an independent evaluator? | review finding 5 | ilp-learners close |\n261\t| IL2-Q4 | IL-R9's learner-timeout clause assumes every learner has one; ILASP 4.4.1 does not | IL2-F5, refuted premise 4 | repair the plan at milestone close |\n262\t| IL1-Q2 | (carried) the non-exporting refusal and `contract` variation | IL2-D7 | IL5 and IL4 |\n263\t\n264\t**Carried rows discharged:** IL1-Q3 (the Popper threshold parser now refuses\n265\tnames the renderer never writes, IL2-D8; out-of-set values stay in IL1's\n266\tboundary). IL1 refuted premise 4 is answered by the ground `thr_` facts and\n267\tdomain-bound rules, which ILASP accepted.\n268\t\n269\t## Refuted premises\n270\t\n271\t1. **\"The macOS ILASP binary is self-contained\"** (spec §12 and IL2-D2). It\n272\t   is false: it links a Homebrew Python 3.10 framework (IL2-F4). Resolved by\n273\t   IL2-D12 (a).\n274\t2. **\"The hypothesis is printed before ILASP's first `%%` line\"** (spec §6).\n275\t   It is false: the timing block comes first (IL2-F5, the probe).\n276\t3. **\"A learned constraint is refused `asp-constraint`\"** (IL2-F5's own\n277\t   claim). It was false until IL2-F8: the corrected extractor still dropped\n278\t   every non-`wrong` line.\n279\t4. **\"The learner has its own timeout below the wall clock\"** (plan IL-R9).\n280\t   It is false for ILASP 4.4.1. Repair: IL2-Q4.\n281\t5. **\"Binding the comparison's variable through `dom_t` keeps ILASP's rule\n282\t   inside GND's fragment\"** (the spec §6 rendering design). It is false:\n283\t   ILASP's cheapest rule is the comparison alone (IL2-F7). Carried as IL2-Q2."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_bFELuvrX8rW4Kdd6uZGrc2mQ","content":"1\t---\n2\tmilestone: ilp-learners\n3\tstation: phase-IL1\n4\tskill: \"n/a -- repository development via process-phase, not a gnd-solve station over a domain model\"\n5\tscope: phase-IL1\n6\tdate: 2026-10-27\n7\tgate:\n8\t  command: \"uv run pytest -q -p no:randomly <the IL1 file list, evidence/IL1/gate-files.txt>\"\n9\t  exit: 0\n10\t  output: \"673 passed, 19 deselected in 41.83s\"\n11\t  note: >-\n12\t    The literal gate of spec §8: the direct IL1 tests (tests/test_ilp_learners.py)\n13\t    and the plan §9 impact closure (the IK5 corpus, the IK6 walk, the IK close\n14\t    test, the RF1 CLI goldens, RF5 commands, the layer map, the architecture\n15\t    test, the RF6 census, the built inventory and schema sync). The live lane\n16\t    ran separately under the scratch SWI and Popper venv: 3 passed. Ruff clean.\n17\tpost_merge:\n18\t  note: >-\n19\t    Merging main (cba51bc) brought the carried-defects RF6 successor in at the\n20\t    same chain position. The IL1 delta was re-chained after it: same rows, new\n21\t    predecessor and hash, totals 6582 distinct rows and 8250 occurrences. The\n22\t    gate above was rerun on the merged tree with the same result, 673 passed,\n23\t    19 deselected; final-gate.txt keeps the pre-merge output.\n24\tslow_cadence:\n25\t  command: \"uv run pytest -q\"\n26\t  trigger: \"explicit owner selection or separately configured CI\"\n27\t  reason: \"outside IL1's impact closure; the reduced v6.3 selection was run\"\n28\tevidence:\n29\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/ilp-learners/notes/phase-IL1-spec.md\n30\t    sha256: 24471087446e282740272317a57a9d06cf584955ff40b9b874c0b817af4302f3\n31\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/ilp-learners/notes/phase-IL1-agent-review.md\n32\t    sha256: 53eeea7b5ca3e42b494413ce5f5f14862f55768a82bedc43e49381e087482275\n33\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/ilp-learners/evidence/IL1/gate-files.txt\n34\t    sha256: 62c8a86be17d2e45