dence/IL1/live/invocation-3/proposal.json\n58\t    sha256: defbeaf0fd62103066cdb42fbf29b8b17b9b2ee9484ec01e72c982432704b02d\n59\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/ilp-learners/evidence/IL1/live/invocation-3/import-report.json\n60\t    sha256: 442e96a368ed520fa04f4812d19061302a7739e29e4833f1001961600f64d131\n61\t  - path: tests/fixtures/ilp_learners/il1/escapes.json\n62\t    sha256: 1ab38d18e6484f28f54d1167751eea5ad0495de85052925acb1d407ba19f15cc\n63\t  - path: tests/fixtures/ilp_learners/il1/joins.json\n64\t    sha256: e284be0c75331a512ebc1cfc906921527e65997ccf7fc78cb0994fe354a01462\n65\t  - path: tests/fixtures/induced_knowledge/ik5-corpus/expected.json\n66\t    sha256: 76931cd3890b0c7f652c625f26354b4bcfcf8d618c32798103a386a37233fc85\n67\t---\n68\t\n69\t# Phase IL1 — the learner registry, the join check, SWI escapes and a real Popper run\n70\t\n71\t**Claim.** IL1-C1 to C5 hold on the evidence below, under:\n72\t- the owner gate in spec §13 (IL1-D1..D9);\n73\t- the IL1-F1 ruling (drop the neutral learner check) and the IL1-F2 ruling\n74\t  (accept SWI's LGPL libgmp for local use), both in spec §14;\n75\t- amendments IL1-A1 (spec §15) and IL1-A2 (spec §16), each approved by the\n76\t  owner on 2026-10-27 before its code changed.\n77\t\n78\t**The headline.** In invocation 3, a real Popper (v5.0.1, commit 578a4e2)\n79\tlearned the refunds tutorial's rule from GND's export:\n80\t\n81\t```prolog\n82\twrong(V0):- f_refund_amount(V0,V1,V2),gt_t_amount__500(V2).\n83\t```\n84\t\n85\tPopper scored it at precision and recall 1.00. SWI over `bk.pl` and GND's\n86\tchecker over the population both cover the same four examples. `gnd import\n87\tilp-rules` admitted it as one guarded constraint, \"amount at most 500\"\n88\t(induced, proposed, deontic, support 4/4). Getting there took two rendering\n89\tamendments, each owner-approved, and three recorded runs.\n90\t\n91\t## What shipped\n92\t\n93\t- **`gnd.export.ilp_learners`** (new). One `Learner` entry per `--target`,\n94\t  in declaration order: renderer, parser, the run record's learner name, the\n95\t  `method` token, the contract, and its own `adapter_version` (IL1-F8).\n96\t  `ilp_service` consults it and names no learner. The command modules keep\n97\t  literal `choices=` tuples (RF5), and T2 pins them and both schema enums to\n98\t  the registry.\n99\t- **Check 9b, `type-confused-join`** (`ilp_rewrite.check_join_types`, D12\n100\t  (o), D13 (o)). A named variable's sites, including a declared comparison's\n101\t  type, must have intersecting ancestor closures (`ilp.type_closures`, from\n102\t  `ModelIndex.supertype_closure`). The import always passes the closures.\n103\t- **SWI escapes in Popper text** (`ilp_popper`). Octal `\\NNN\\` (1 to 7\n104\t  digits) and, after review finding 7, every form SWI 10.0.2's `writeq`\n105\t  writes: `\\a \\b \\v \\f \\r`, `\\xN\\`. Refusals are `unparsable` with a line\n106\t  and column; one helper builds them all (the executed refactor).\n107\t- **`extract_program`** reads Popper v5.0.1's stderr log (IL1-F4): the first\n108\t  run of rules after the last solution banner, prefixes stripped (anchored\n109\t  after review finding 4a).\n110\t- **The Popper rendering, adapter version 3** (IL1-A1, IL1-A2):\n111\t  - `bk.pl` is grouped by predicate;\n112\t  - each comparison against an observed integer value is a unary threshold\n113\t    predicate (`gt`, `lt`; at most 32 values per type, ranked selection),\n114\t    written as ground facts over the exported values it holds for;\n115\t  - thresholds that hold for no value are omitted;\n116\t  - `bias.pl` lists them, with no binary comparison and no\n117\t    `magic_value_type`;\n118\t  - the parser maps a threshold atom back to the declared binary comparison,\n119\t    so checks 5 and 9b apply unchanged.\n120\t\n121\t  The neutral target stays at adapter version 1.\n122\t- **The evidence script** `evidence/IL1/run_popper.py`. It runs Popper under\n123\t  `run_bounded_process` with all six limits, has SWI evaluate coverage\n124\t  independently, imports with fixed arguments and sanitizes paths. The\n125\t  install is a hash-pinned lock in a scratch prefix.\n126\t\n127\t**Goldens that moved, all by owner amendment:**\n128\t- the X1 Popper export tree;\n129\t- in `expected.json`, E for the Popper target and I2's provenance digests;\n130\t- the `export_sha256` field of 19 IK5 run records.\n131\t\n132\tNo IK5 exit code or refusal changed. No IK5 case became `type-confused-join`.\n133\tThe neutral target, the IK6 walk and the RF1 goldens are unchanged.\n134\t\n135\t## Gate output (verbatim)\n136\t\n137\tFrom `evidence/IL1/final-gate.txt` (the scratch path replaced by `<scratch>`):\n138\t\n139\t```\n140\t$ uv run pytest -q -p no:randomly $(cat .gnd-planning/milestones/ilp-learners/evidence/IL1/gate-files.txt)\n141\t673 passed, 19 deselected in 41.83s\n142\texit 0\n143\t$ GND_IL1_SWIPL=<scratch>/SWI-Prolog.app/Contents/MacOS/swipl GND_IL1_POPPER_PYTHON=<scratch>/venv/bin/python uv run pytest -q -p no:randomly -m live tests/test_ilp_learners.py\n144\t3 passed, 50 deselected in 0.45s\n145\texit 0\n146\t$ uv run ruff check src/gnd/export tests/test_ilp_learners.py .gnd-planning/milestones/ilp-learners/evidence/IL1/run_popper.py\n147\tAll checks passed!\n148\texit 0\n149\t```\n150\t\n151\tEvery regression test for a review fix was observed red against `ed54e65`\n152\tbefore its fix, and A2-T3 and A2-T4 were observed red against adapter 2's\n153\tcode (spec §16).\n154\t\n155\t## The three recorded runs\n156\t\n157\t| Invocation | Rendering | Termination | Import | What it settled |\n158\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n159\t| 1, **the run of record** | IK5 (adapter 1) | `rendering-rejected` (exit 1, 18.0 s) | `none` | v5.0.1 has no magic values, so a binary comparison's constant is unbound and arithmetic raises (IL1-F7) |\n160\t| 2 | adapter 2: rule-defined thresholds | `completed` (1.2 s), `NO SOLUTION` | `none` | the crash is gone, but clingo grounds the rules with no atoms and Popper bans every threshold; its pointless-relation query also sees them all as equivalent (IL1-F9, closed by review finding 2) |\n161\t| 3 | adapter 3: ground-fact thresholds | `completed` (1.2 s) | `admitted` | the headline above |\n162\t\n163\tT9 replays all three from their committed bytes in the default gate. For\n164\tinvocation 3 that includes the import, the normalized report and the\n165\tproposal's bytes.\n166\t\n167\t**The spec's three live-run questions** (§6), answered by invocation 3:\n168\t1. **Does Popper accept the rendering?** Adapter 3: yes. Adapters 1 and 2: no\n169\t   (rows above).\n170\t2. **Does the output parse and import?** Yes: exit 0, admitted.\n171\t3. **Does every learned clause fit the induction block without loss (the IK2\n172\t   residual)?** For this one clause, yes. Its `provenance.induction` carries\n173\t   the inducer, the method, the examples, support 4/4 and the export,\n174\t   clauses and run digests. One clause is one clause.\n175\t\n176\t## Criteria\n177\t\n178\t| Criterion | Result |\n179\t|---|---|\n180\t| IL1-C1 registry | holds: T2, T3 (the fake entry reaches the tree, method and learner check), T3b; the service has no learner literal |\n181\t| IL1-C2 join check | holds: T5 J1–J4, T5b, T5c, T5e, T5f, A1-T5 (a threshold of another integer type). T5d's neutral learner rule was dropped by the IL1-F1 ruling |\n182\t| IL1-C3 escapes | holds: T4, T4b, and test_r7 over every escape form SWI 10.0.2 writes, recorded in the review |\n183\t| IL1-C4 live run | holds: invocation 1 is the run of record, with one termination and one import value; T9 replays it, and invocations 2 and 3 are reported beside it |\n184\t| IL1-C5 join space | holds: T11, a stand-in learner join candidate that imports with exit 0 |\n185\t\n186\t## Refactoring review\n187\t\n188\t**Executed:**\n189\t- **One `unparsable` refusal** (`b906749`). The Popper parser built the same\n190\t  \"unparsable: line L, column C\" error in five places, and the threshold\n191\t  mapping reached into the parser class for it. One module helper now builds\n192\t  it. Messages are unchanged, and the gate is green.\n193\t\n194\t**Seen and deferred** (open questions below):\n195\t- the service does not enforce `Learner.exports` (review finding 6);\n196\t- `Learner.contract` has one value, so it is a field no code path varies on\n197\t  yet.\n198\t\n199\tIL2 adds the second real adapter, which is where both become real\n200\tdecisions.\n201\t\n202\t**Not refactored, argued:**\n203\t- **`ilp.ADAPTER_VERSION`** now means only the neutral target's version. It\n204\t  stays as the default of `export_tree` so that IK5's imports of\n205\t  `export_tree` keep working; the registry carries every target's actual\n206\t  version.\n207\t- **`_threshold_rows`** re-reads the neutral facts that `build_neutral` has\n208\t  just written. It is a second pass over in-memory data, not a second\n209\t  definition of anything. Its single consumer is `render`.\n210\t\n211\t## Boundary — what this phase does NOT establish\n212\t\n213\t- **One reviewer is one reviewer.**\n214\t  - The adversarial review was one local agent over `git diff 5576a4e ed54e65`.\n215\t  - It did not run Popper or the full suite.\n216\t  - The amendment-2 code and the refactor carry no review opinion.\n217\t- **Reproducibility is not measured.** Each invocation is a single run.\n218\t  Invocation 3's success is one run of one learner on one eight-example\n219\t  tutorial dataset.\n220\t- **Rule quality is not established.** Invocation 3 shows that the bridge\n221\t  carries a real learner's output end to end. It says nothing about whether\n222\t  Popper finds good rules on other data, or about the threshold selection's\n223\t  effect on larger domains (above 32 values, rules can only use the selected\n224\t  thresholds).\n225\t- **Meaning is preserved only over the exported values.** A threshold's\n226\t  ground facts equal its comparison only over the values in the export. The\n227\t  import re-checks coverage with GND's own comparison over the population, so\n228\t  an admitted clause's coverage is GND's, not the facts'.\n229\t- **Popper's other settings are not covered.** Only the settings in spec §6\n230\t  were exercised; noise, recursion, `direction` and predicate invention were\n231\t  not.\n232\t- **The infix comparison gap stays open.** An infix comparison across two\n233\t  integer types is admitted while the same comparison written as a predicate\n234\t  is refused (review finding 3). IK5 behaved the same way.\n235\t- **The neutral target accepts any learner name** (the IL1-F1 residual).\n236\t- **Spec T6 is a deviation.** It named `tests/test_ilp_live.py`, which does\n237\t  not exist. The live checks are in `tests/test_ilp_learners.py` under the\n238\t  `live` marker (A1-T2, A2-T3, A2-T4), and the runs are the evidence script.\n239\t- **SWI-Prolog's LGPL libgmp** is accepted for local scratch use only\n240\t  (IL1-F2); nothing is distributed.\n241\t- **The broad historical lane did not run** (`slow_cadence`).\n242\t\n243\t## Open questions\n244\t\n245\t| ID | Question | Origin | Target |\n246\t|---|---|---|---|\n247\t| IL1-Q1 | Should an infix comparison take part in check 9b like a declared comparison predicate? It changes IK5 behaviour | review finding 3 | IL4, which owns the join check's next call |\n248\t| IL1-Q2 | Should the service refuse a non-exporting entry, and should `contract` vary? | review finding 6; refactoring review | IL2, the second real adapter |\n249\t| IL1-Q3 | Should the threshold parser refuse names the renderer never writes (leading zeros, `m0`, values outside the export's set)? | review finding 5 | IL2 |\n250\t| IL1-Q4 | `extract_program` stops at the first non-rule line inside a solution block, without reporting the truncation | review finding 4b | ilp-learners close |\n251\t| IL1-Q5 | Missing tests: T5c's pair count, and a `type_closures` subtype test | review finding 8 | ilp-learners close |\n252\t| IL1-Q6 | Is Popper's success reproducible, and does it hold on a larger domain? | boundary | IL6 or a later evaluation phase |\n253\t| IL1-Q7 | The plan's §9 IL1 row says \"goldens unchanged except listed C2 cases\"; the amendments moved IK5 goldens (refuted premise 2) | this record | repair the plan at milestone close |\n254\t\n255\t**Carried rows discharged:** IK5-Q5 (a real Popper run, and whether its\n256\toutput fits the IK2 block) and IK5-Q2 (SWI octal escapes) are answered here.\n257\t\n258\t## Refuted premises\n259\t\n260\t1. **\"Every IK5 golden is unchanged except type-confused clauses\" with a\n261\t   neutral learner check** (spec §5 against IL1-C2). It is false: 13 approved\n262\t   neutral imports would turn exit 3. Killed by IL1-F1 against the IK5 corpus,\n263\t   and resolved by the owner dropping the check.\n264\t2. **The plan's \"goldens unchanged except listed C2 cases\" for IL1** (plan\n265\t   §9). It is false once the live run demanded rendering amendments; IL1-A1\n266\t   and IL1-A2 moved IK5 goldens by owner ruling. Repair: IL1-Q7.\n267\t3. **\"The IK5 Popper rendering works with a real Popper\"** (open since\n268\t   IK5-D13). It is false for v5.0.1: invocation 1 (IL1-F7).\n269\t4. **\"A rule-defined threshold that fails on an unbound argument is safe for\n270\t   Popper\"** (IL1-A1's design). It is false: Popper's clingo grounding and\n271\t   its pointless-relation query both need ground facts. Killed by invocation\n272\t   2 and review finding 2."}
