s/ilp_learners/il3/expected/refunds/export.json\n81\t    sha256: 7b455e99b224d1c7ab41fd2bcfdd1eb10914e795f57d2dd8e5b1c0494a2e5827\n82\t  - path: tests/fixtures/ilp_learners/il3/expected/refunds/features.json\n83\t    sha256: f96c151bfcb3c846f63e245f02aaf09d3fc57e7a85e316e59e9e022e031f72d3\n84\t---\n85\t\n86\t# Phase IL3 — Boolean rule sets: a feature table out, a rule set back, one RIPPER run\n87\t\n88\t**Claim.** IL3-C1 to C4 hold on the evidence below, under:\n89\t- the owner's gate rulings of 2026-10-28 (spec §13);\n90\t- the owner's ruling on IL3-F2, \"Arity in the name\" (spec §14);\n91\t- one reviewer's adversarial read, whose 8 findings were all reproduced; 7\n92\t  were fixed and 1 is an open question for the owner (IL3-Q1).\n93\t\n94\t## What shipped\n95\t\n96\t- **`src/gnd/export/ilp_rules.py` (new):**\n97\t  - `render(neutral)` writes `rules/features.json`, `gnd-ilp-features/1`:\n98\t    one row per example, one 0/1 column per (integer argument position,\n99\t    Popper threshold row). The column name spells its clause:\n100\t    `<predicate>__<position>__<arity>__<comparison>__<threshold>`.\n101\t  - **Export refusals:** `no-features`, `too-many-features` (over 4,096),\n102\t    `too-large` (over 4,000,000 cells), `column-name` (a name over 160\n103\t    characters, a threshold over 32 digits, or an id that does not read back\n104\t    as itself).\n105\t  - `parse_ruleset(text)` reads wittgenstein's printed rule set. The polarity\n106\t    table refuses `ordered-rule-list`, `empty-antecedent`,\n107\t    `negation-as-failure` and `propositional-conjunction` by name; a single\n108\t    true feature becomes its clause with fresh variables. Caps: 32 rules, 16\n109\t    conditions, 160-character names, arity 64, 32-digit thresholds.\n110\t  - `extract_ruleset(stdout)`, shared by the run script and T9.\n111\t- **`src/gnd/ilp-features.schema.json` (new),** in both schema inventories.\n112\t- **The registry entry `rules`** (learner `wittgenstein`, method\n113\t  `ilp-rules`); the `gnd export ilp` and `gnd import ilp-rules` choices and\n114\t  help texts; both `target` enums, widened within `/1`; the layer map.\n115\t- **RF1:** the ILP help and exit goldens and `cli/tree.json`, re-captured\n116\t  under Python 3.11, 3.13 and 3.14. `gnd export ilp`'s goldens are now stored\n117\t  per version, because 3.11 wraps its usage line differently. The manifest\n118\t  lines and `MANIFEST_SHA256` moved with them.\n119\t- **RF6:** `evidence/IL3/dynamic-query-successor.json`, 23 added syntax rows,\n120\t  chained after IL5's.\n121\t- **`docs/reference/ilp-bridge.md`:** a \"Boolean rule sets\" section, and a\n122\t  files-table row; the LLM section's extraction sentence now states IL5-Q2's\n123\t  ruling (any stray fence makes no answer).\n124\t- **Evidence:**\n125\t  - `evidence/live_common.py` (new), the shared live-run helper (IL5-Q4,\n126\t    IL3-D10);\n127\t  - `evidence/IL3/`: `learn_rules.py` (the driver), `run_rules.py` (the\n128\t    script), `downloads.json`, `sdist-members.txt`, `probe/`,\n129\t    `live/invocation-1/`, `review-brief.md`, `final-gate.txt`.\n130\t- **Tests:** `tests/test_ilp_rules.py` (78 default-lane cases and one live),\n131\t  over the corpus `tests/fixtures/ilp_learners/il3/`.\n132\t\n133\t## Gate output (verbatim)\n134\t\n135\tFrom `evidence/IL3/final-gate.txt`:\n136\t\n137\t```\n138\t$ uv run pytest -q -p no:randomly $(cat .gnd-planning/milestones/ilp-learners/evidence/IL3/gate-files.txt)\n139\t959 passed, 23 deselected in 170.28s (0:02:50)\n140\t$ GND_IL3_PYTHON=<scratch>/venv/bin/python GND_IL3_LEARNER=<scratch>/wittgenstein-0.3.5 uv run pytest -q -p no:randomly -m live tests/test_ilp_rules.py\n141\t1 passed, 78 deselected in 2.16s\n142\t$ uv run ruff check src/gnd/export src/gnd/commands tests/test_ilp_rules.py .gnd-planning/milestones/ilp-learners/evidence/live_common.py .gnd-planning/milestones/ilp-learners/evidence/IL3\n143\tAll checks passed!\n144\t$ <scratch>/venv311/bin/python -m pytest -q -p no:randomly tests/test_rf1_cli_pins.py tests/test_rf1_pin_harness.py   # Python 3.11.15\n145\t152 passed in 18.12s\n146\t$ <scratch>/venv313/bin/python -m pytest -q -p no:randomly tests/test_rf1_cli_pins.py tests/test_rf1_pin_harness.py   # Python 3.13.12\n147\t152 passed in 24.60s\n148\t$ uv run pytest -q -p no:randomly tests/test_rf1_pin_harness.py -k golden_manifest\n149\t4 passed, 35 deselected in 0.26s\n150\t```\n151\t\n152\t`slow_cadence` (`uv run pytest -q`) did not run: it is outside IL3's impact\n153\tclosure and stays an explicit owner selection.\n154\t\n155\t## The run of record\n156\t\n157\tInvocation 1, `evidence/IL3/live/invocation-1/`:\n158\t- **termination** `completed`; **import** `admitted`, exit 0;\n159\t- E = `7b455e99…5827`;\n160\t- **the learner:** wittgenstein 0.3.5, `RIPPER(random_state=0,\n161\t  n_discretize_bins=None)`, on the local CPython 3.13.12 with numpy 2.5.4,\n162\t  pandas 3.1.0, python-dateutil 3.0.0, six 1.17.0 and tzdata 2026.6. Those\n163\t  versions are the only files the venv was installed from (`--no-index`,\n164\t  `downloads.json`); `outcome.json` itself does not list them (review 8);\n165\t- **the rule set:** `[[f_refund_amount__2__3__gt_t_amount__450=1]]`, that is\n166\t  `wrong(X) :- f_refund_amount(X, V1, V2), gt_t_amount(V2, 450)`;\n167\t- **coverage:** the learner's own `Rule.covers` gives airport, harbor,\n168\t  market, south and station; GND computes the same 5, with support 4/5\n169\t  (`south` is labelled `neg`). The rule is admitted as a proposed, advisory\n170\t  constraint with that support recorded.\n171\t\n172\t**The three questions the spec asked:**\n173\t1. Does wittgenstein accept the table? Yes: the probe and invocation 1 both\n174\t   ran with empty stderr.\n175\t2. Does the rule set parse and import? Yes, admitted.\n176\t3. Does the learner's coverage agree with GND's? Yes, set for set.\n177\t\n178\t**Not repeatable (IL3-F5).** RIPPER 0.3.5 picks a different threshold on\n179\trepeated runs, even with `random_state=0` and a fixed hash seed. 11\n180\tdiagnostic re-runs, made beyond the one approved run and disclosed in the\n181\tspec, gave 500, 450 and 310. Invocation 1 is the run of record as recorded.\n182\t\n183\t## Criteria\n184\t\n185\t| Criterion | Holds | By |\n186\t|---|---|---|\n187\t| IL3-C1: the table is golden across two hash seeds; the bounds are fixed before results; the work counter stays under its ceiling | yes | T1 (two models, two seeds), T2 (oracle), T3 (each bound at and one over) |\n188\t| IL3-C2: each polarity row has a test per spelling; a positive single feature maps to a clause that re-checks | yes | T4 (26 corpus cases), T5 (admitted), R7 |\n189\t| IL3-C3: the coverage re-check compares the learner's per-rule sets with GND's, from the learner's own predict | yes | T6 (`coverage-mismatch`), T9, T-live |\n190\t| IL3-C4: one live run under IL-R9, with a replay test | yes | invocation 1; T9 (with R6's tamper cases) |\n191\t\n192\t## Review\n193\t\n194\tOne reviewer is one reviewer: one local agent read `git diff e30eec8\n195\t620f394`. Its report is retained, edited only to replace paths, in\n196\t`notes/phase-IL3-agent-review.md`, with the disposition. All 8 findings were\n197\treproduced:\n198\t- **1 blocking, fixed:** an unbounded arity in a column name let a 46-byte\n199\t  rule set make the import allocate without limit.\n200\t- **3 hardening, fixed:** the renderer could write names its reader refuses;\n201\t  it refused with an undocumented name; the shared helper mapped unruled\n202\t  process statuses.\n203\t- **1 hardening, for the owner:** IL3-Q1.\n204\t- **3 completeness, fixed:** T9's blind spots, the at-bound reader cases, and\n205\t  the help and docs drift. One part stays open: outcome.json does not list\n206\t  the pandas and numpy versions (above).\n207\t\n208\tThe reviewer did not run the learner or the run script, and did not run the\n209\tfull suite.\n210\t\n211\t**Coverage audit against the declared branches:**\n212\t- **