lose/red.txt`) | recorded |\n120\t| C1–C9 | pass |\n121\t| C10 every retained run replays (IL1–IL6 replay tests, in the gate) | pass |\n122\t| C11 the comparison tool exits 0; the walk passes its 12 blocks | pass |\n123\t| T8 RF1 pins, RF5, layering, arch, RF6 (an IL-close census successor), built inventory, schema sync, API pins | pass (in the gate) |\n124\t| T9 both wheel origins | pass |\n125\t\n126\t## Review\n127\t\n128\t`notes/phase-IL-close-agent-review.md`, retained (scratch prefix scrubbed).\n129\t1 blocking, 4 hardening, 2 completeness; every finding reproduced and fixed,\n130\teach with a regression shown red before its fix (`evidence/IL-close/review-red.txt`).\n131\t\n132\t| # | Finding | Class | Disposition |\n133\t|---|---|---|---|\n134\t| 1 | An own-reference subtype shared its supertype's family; Integer `1` and String `\"1\"` met and the import exited 70 | blocking | fixed, R1 (ILC-F8) |\n135\t| 2 | A cyclic hierarchy fell back to per-type names | hardening | fixed, R2 |\n136\t| 3 | An undeclared ILASP comparison was named `off-threshold` | hardening | fixed, R3 |\n137\t| 4 | The re-render could refuse `no-relations` ahead of `facts-mismatch` | hardening | fixed, R4 |\n138\t| 5 | The comparison tool tracebacked with exit 1 on unparsable rules | hardening | fixed, R5 |\n139\t| 6 | `facts-mismatch`'s order was untested | completeness | fixed, R6 (red against the reviewer's mutant) |\n140\t| 7 | The page said facts are checked \"before any rule is read\" | completeness | fixed |\n141\t\n142\t## Refactoring review\n143\t\n144\t**None executed.** The part touched one function in each of six bridge\n145\tmodules, the tool and the evidence; each change is a local repair whose\n146\tneighbours were already shaped for it (the registry took a hook rather than a\n147\tlearner name; the join check took a second loop over the sites it already\n148\tbuilt). One structural point is deferred:\n149\t\n150\t- **The mined import renders the facts twice.** The `facts-mismatch` check\n151\t  calls `ilp_amie.render`, then the import builds the relation table and the\n152\t  spelled pairs again for the count. One shared pass would serve both. The\n153\t  cost is bounded by the export's fact cap, so it is left for the milestone\n154\t  that owns the bridge's performance (IL-close-Q1).\n155\t\n156\t## Boundary -- what this part does NOT establish\n157\t\n158\t- **That an own-reference subtype's joins are counted.** They are refused\n159\t  `support-mismatch`, as before IL-close: a false refusal, never an admission.\n160\t  Whether raw values identify entities across such a subtype is a modelling\n161\t  question.\n162\t- **Clause order of refusals for ILASP.** The threshold check runs over every\n163\t  clause before the rewrite (§6.5), so a later clause's `off-threshold`\n164\t  outranks an earlier clause's rewrite refusal. Both refuse the set.\n165\t- **Any learner behaviour.** No learner ran; the retained runs were re-derived.\n166\t- **The milestone's close.** Parts B to E (plan repairs, the question sweep,\n167\t  the four-reviewer review, the close record) follow.\n168\t\n169\t## Open questions\n170\t\n171\t| Id | Question | Owner | Target |\n172\t|---|---|---|---|\n173\t| ILC-F5 | IL1's test r5 pinned a bare `true` at a string role as the string; under IL2-Q1 it is the boolean. Accept the moved assertion? | owner | **accepted 2026-10-29** |\n174\t| ILC-F6 | Moves beyond spec §8: the IL4 `export.json` goldens (`adapter_version` 2), invocation 2's `import-report.json`, walk block 10 (not 9), T9's adapter-version assertion, `run_amie.py`. Accept? | owner | **accepted 2026-10-29** |\n175\t| IL-close-Q1 | Share one rendering pass between `facts-mismatch` and the count | owner | later milestone |\n176\t\n177\t**Owner ruling, 2026-10-29,** quoted: \"I accept ILC-F5 and ILC-F6 as\n178\trecorded. Continue with close parts B to E.\" Recorded after this record's\n179\tcommit `d6c70c7`; the rest of the record is unchanged.\n180\t\n181\t## 